<p>If you are just starting with local SEO, begin with Claire Carlile and Phil Rozek. Their content is accessible and foundational. If you are dealing with a specific Google Business Profile issue, Joy Hawkins, Ben Fisher, and Colan Nielsen are your best resources. For technical implementation, turn to Tom Waddington. For strategic growth, Mary Bowling and Carrie Hill offer the big-picture perspective.</p>
<h3>Engage with Their Communities</h3>
<p>Many of these experts are active on Twitter/X and LinkedIn. Following them there gives you access to real-time insights, discussions, and the ability to ask questions. The Local Search Forum, founded by Joy Hawkins, is particularly valuable for getting answers to specific local SEO questions from experts and peers.</p>
<h3>Attend Their Events</h3>
<p>LocalU conferences, MozCon, SMX, and Pubcon feature many of these speakers. Attending — or watching recordings — gives you access to their latest thinking in a concentrated format. The Q&amp;A sessions at these events often surface insights that never make it into blog posts.</p>
